The failure localizes cleanly: the planner compares pathname `lstat()` metadata byte-for-byte with descriptor `fstat()` metadata before hashing. Windows can expose different-but-equivalent fields across those two APIs, producing the false “changed while opening” result. I’m checking the exact Python/Windows semantics before choosing the identity comparison, then I’ll encode them in a regression test rather than weakening the later before/after change check.
