I’ve confirmed the exact version split from the failed run: Python 3.11 only exposes the PATH-fixture failures, while Windows Python 3.12+ also fails because pathname stat reports legacy creation-time `st_ctime` and descriptor stat reports change-time `st_ctime`. I’m adding an end-to-end simulated regression for that split and a shared native-name PATH helper that keeps `git` discoverable while proving `go` is absent.
